ould've made it more clear, but I meant in the build with the changes from the PR","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3115674457/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3117132412","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108855#issuecomment-3117132412","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108855","id":3117132412,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc65y6p8","user":{"login":"OS-of-S","id":171816144,"node_id":"U_kgDOCj200A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/171816144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/OS-of-S","html_url":"https://github.com/OS-of-S","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OS-of-S/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OS-of-S/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OS-of-S/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OS-of-S/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OS-of-S/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OS-of-S/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OS-of-S/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OS-of-S/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OS-of-S/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-25T09:52:56Z","updated_at":"2025-07-25T10:02:01Z","body":"> Should've made it more clear, but I meant in the build with the changes from the PR\r\n\r\nAw... Sorry. Was tired. I tried your branch on my exemple, and it really worked now!\r\n\r\n<img width=\"792\" height=\"235\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/950568c1-dd0f-46d3-a78f-70e372a8cc59\" />\r\n\r\nHope to see it finished and merged. It gives me some errors in console, connected to reparenting, for some reason, and we still need to keep in mind [another bug related to physics update of CharacterBody and AnimatableBody](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/76256) that needs an additional workaround with single `await get_tree().physics_frame`, but it worked!\r\n\r\nJust to note: Area's behaviour very unintuitive. For exemple, when I reparent whole scene with area and bodies inside it, it still emits exit and enter signals for them even if nothing but hierarchy is changed. I understand why is that so, and it's not connected with the discussed bug, but it's just very unintuitive.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3117132412/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3117195923","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108855#issuecomment-3117195923","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108855","id":3117195923,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc65zKKT","user":{"login":"mlm-games","id":125530737,"node_id":"U_kgDOB3tycQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/125530737?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlm-games","html_url":"https://github.com/mlm-games","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlm-games/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlm-games/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlm-games/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlm-games/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlm-games/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlm-games/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlm-games/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlm-games/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlm-games/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-25T10:15:10Z","updated_at":"2025-07-25T10:17:57Z","body":"> > Should've made it more clear, but I meant in the build with the changes from the PR\r\n> \r\n> Aw... Sorry. Was tired. I tried your branch on my exemple, and it really worked now!\r\n> <img alt=\"image\" width=\"792\" height=\"235\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/171816144/470712851-950568c1-dd0f-46d3-a78f-70e372a8cc59.png?jwt=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3NTM0Mzg1OTksIm5iZiI6MTc1MzQzODI5OSwicGF0aCI6Ii8xNzE4MTYxNDQvNDcwNzEyODUxLTk1MDU2OGMxLWRkMGYtNDZkMy1hNzhmLTcwZTM3MmE4Y2M1OS5wbmc_.597CPAIEQ1Vd50jFrOnj7B9LNlwCSMsl8E52QbR7ZOw\">\r\n> \r\n> Hope to see it finished and merged. It gives me some errors in console, connected to reparenting, for some reason, and we still need to keep in mind [another bug related to physics update of CharacterBody and AnimatableBody](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/76256) that needs an additional workaround with single `await get_tree().physics_frame`, but it worked!\r\n> \r\n> Just to note: Area's behaviour very unintuitive. For exemple, when I reparent whole scene with area and bodies inside it, it still emits exit and enter signals for them even if nothing but hierarchy is changed. I understand why is that so, and it's not connected with the discussed bug, but it's just very unintuitive.\r\n\r\n\r\nWell thats good to hear but about the other errors, could you provide a test project or provide more context on the errors, i'll just open it up for review incase the maintainers have anything to say regarding it","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3117195923/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3120405739","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108855#issuecomment-3120405739","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108855","id":3120405739,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc65_Zzr","user":{"login":"OS-of-S","id":171816144,"node_id":"U_kgDOCj200A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/171816144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/OS-of-S","html_url":"https://github.com/OS-of-S","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OS-of-S/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OS-of-S/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OS-of-S/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OS-of-S/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OS-of-S/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OS-of-S/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OS-of-S/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OS-of-S/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OS-of-S/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-25T21:23:22Z","updated_at":"2025-07-25T21:23:22Z","body":"I checked twice and it seems that those errors was my fault, becouse they existed in both your branch and in 4.4 stable. As the error message suggested, I was needed to call reparent as deferred: \"Can't change this state while flushing queries.\"\r\n\r\nI fixed it and made several tests. I am attaching a file. There is only one scene with all scripts build-in (sorry for this bad practice...) Inside Area's script there is several functions: test_1, test_2, test_3 and test_4 with some comments on it. All thouse tests works the same: just moves nodes of different PhysicsBody classes inside Area, then moves them on distance, reparent and counts entering-signal emits. Differences between tests I noted more detailed in comments inside script.\r\n\r\n[area_reparent_testing.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21437694/area_reparent_testing.zip)\r\n\r\nI don't have the necessary knowledge to evaluate the code itself and how correct it is in relation to the engine's physics requirements. It makes sense to tag one of the maintainers who is responsible for this, I think.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3120405739/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3120980543","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108855#issuecomment-3120980543","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108855","id":3120980543,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc66BmI_","user":{"login":"mlm-games","id":125530737,"node_id":"U_kgDOB3tycQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/125530737?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlm-games","html_url":"https://github.com/mlm-games","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlm-games/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlm-games/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlm-games/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlm-games/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlm-games/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlm-games/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlm-games/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlm-games/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mlm-games/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-26T02:02:14Z","updated_at":"2025-07-29T14:44:47Z","body":"> I checked twice and it seems that those errors was my fault, becouse they existed in both your branch and in 4.4 stable. As the error message suggested, I was needed to call reparent as deferred: \"Can't change this state while flushing queries.\"\r\n> \r\n> I fixed it and made several tests. I am attaching a file. There is only one scene with all scripts build-in (sorry for this bad practice...) Inside Area's script there is several functions: test_1, test_2, test_3 and test_4 with some comments on it. All thouse tests works the same: just moves nodes of different PhysicsBody classes inside Area, then moves them on distance, reparent and counts entering-signal emits. Differences between tests I noted more detailed in comments inside script.\r\n> \r\n> [area_reparent_testing.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21437694/area_reparent_testing.zip)\r\n> \r\n> I don't have the necessary knowledge to evaluate the code itself and how correct it is in relation to the engine's physics requirements. It makes sense to tag one of the maintainers who is responsible for this, I think.\r\n\r\nOh that's fine, I am thankful for your testing though. I did request a review from the code owners so have to wait till for their response..","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3120980543/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3170472758","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108855#issuecomment-3170472758","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108855","id":3170472758,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc68-ZM2","user":{"log